H6800.definition:
a primitive root;
to humiliate
KJV: humbly, lowly.

H6801.definition:
a primitive root;
to wrap, i.e. roll or dress
KJV: be attired, [idiom] surely, violently turn.

H6802.definition:
from H6801 (צָנַף);
a ball
KJV: [idiom] toss.

H6803.definition:
from the same as H6791 (צֵן);
a vase (probably a vial tapering at the top)
KJV: pot.

H6804.definition:
probably from the same as H6794 (צִנּוּר);
a tube
KJV: pipe.

H6805.definition:
a primitive root;
to pace, i.e. step regularly; (upward) to mount; (along) to march; (down and causatively) to hurl
KJV: bring, go, march (through), run over.

H6806.definition:
from H6804 (צַנְתָּרָה);
a pace or regular step
KJV: pace, step.

H6807.definition:
feminine of H6806 (צַעַד);
a march; (concretely) an (ornamental) ankle-chain
KJV: going, ornament of the legs.

H6808.definition:
a primitive root;
to tip over (for the purpose of spilling or pouring out), i.e. (figuratively) depopulate; by implication, to imprison or conquer; (reflexive) to lie down (for coitus)
KJV: captive exile, travelling, (cause to) wander(-er).

H6809.definition:
from an unused root meaning to wrap over;
a veil
KJV: vail.

H6810.definition:
or צָעוֹר; from H6819 (צָעַר);
little; (in number) few; (in age) young, (in value) ignoble
KJV: least, little (one), small (one), [phrase] young(-er, -est).

H6811.definition:
the same as H6810 (צָעִיר);
Tsair, a place in Idumaea
KJV: Zair.

H6812.definition:
feminine of H6810 (צָעִיר);
smallness (of age), i.e. juvenility
KJV: youth.

H6813.definition:
a primitive root;
to load up (beasts), i.e. to migrate
KJV: be taken down.

H6814.definition:
of Egyptian derivation;
Tsoan, a place in Egypt
KJV: Zoan.

H6815.definition:
or (dual) צַעֲנַיִם; plural from H6813 (צָעַן); removals;
Tsaanannim or Tsaanajim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zaannannim, Zaanaim.

H6816.definition:
from an unused root meaning to bestrew with carvings;
sculpture
KJV: image (work).

H6817.definition:
a primitive root;
to shriek; (by implication) to proclaim (an assembly)
KJV: [idiom] at all, call together, cry (out), gather (selves) (together).

H6818.definition:
from H6817 (צָעַק);
a shriek
KJV: cry(-ing).

H6819.definition:
a primitive root;
to be small, i.e. (figuratively) ignoble
KJV: be brought low, little one, be small.

H6820.definition:
from H6819 (צָעַר); little;
Tsoar, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Zoar.

H6821.definition:
a primitive root;
to adhere
KJV: cleave.

H6822.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to lean forward, i.e. to peer into the distance; by implication, to observe, await
KJV: behold, espy, look up (well), wait for, (keep the) watch(-man).

H6823.definition:
a primitive root (probably identical with H6822 (צָפָה) through the idea of expansion in outlook, transferring to action);
to sheet over (especially with metal)
KJV: cover, overlay.

H6824.definition:
from H6823 (צָפָה);
an inundation (as covering)
KJV: [idiom] swimmest.

H6825.definition:
or צְפִי; from H6822 (צָפָה); observant;
Tsepho or Tsephi, an Idumaean
KJV: Zephi, Zepho.

H6826.definition:
from H6823 (צָפָה);
encasement (with metal)
KJV: covering, overlaying.

H6827.definition:
probably for H6837 (צִפְיוֹן);
Tsephon, an Israelite
KJV: Zephon.

H6828.definition:
or צָפֹן; from H6845 (צָפַן);
properly, hidden, i.e. dark; used only of the north as aquarter (gloomy and unknown)
KJV: north(-ern, side, -ward, wind).

H6829.definition:
the same as H6828 (צָפוֹן); boreal;
Tsaphon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zaphon.

H6831.definition:
patronymically from H6827 (צְפוֹן);
a Tsephonite, or (collectively) descendants of Tsephon
KJV: Zephonites.

H6832.definition:
from the same as H6848 (צֶפַע);
excrement (as protruded)
KJV: dung.

H6833.definition:
or צִפֹּר; from H6852 (צָפַר);
a little bird (as hopping)
KJV: bird, fowl, sparrow.

H6834.definition:
the same as H6833 (צִפּוֹר);
Tsippor, a Moabite
KJV: Zippor.

H6835.definition:
from an unused root meaning to expand;
a saucer (as flat)
KJV: cruse.

H6837.definition:
from H6822 (צָפָה); watch-tower;
Tsiphjon, an Israelite
KJV: Ziphion. Compare H6827 (צְפוֹן).

H6838.definition:
from the same as H6835 (צַפַּחַת);
a flat thin cake
KJV: wafer.

H6839.definition:
plural of active participle of H6822 (צָפָה); watchers;
Tsophim, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Zophim.

H6840.definition:
from H6845 (צָפַן);
a treasure (as hidden)
KJV: hid.

H6841.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6842 (צָפִיר);
a he-goat
KJV: he (goat).

H6842.definition:
from H6852 (צָפַר);
a male goat (as prancing)
KJV: (he) goat.

H6843.definition:
feminine formed like H6842 (צָפִיר);
a crown (as encircling the head); also a turn of affairs (i.e. mishap)
KJV: diadem, morning.

H6844.definition:
from H6822 (צָפָה);
a sentry
KJV: watchtower.

H6845.definition:
a primitive root;
to hide (by covering over); by implication, to hoard or reserve; figuratively to deny; specifically (favorably) to protect, (unfavorably) to lurk
KJV: esteem, hide(-den one, self), lay up, lurk (be set) privily, (keep) secret(-ly, place).

H6846.definition:
or צְפַנְיָהוּ; from H6845 (צָפַן) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has secreted;
Tsephanjah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Zephaniah.

H6847.definition:
of Egyptian derivation;
Tsophnath-Paneach, Joseph's Egyptian name
KJV: Zaphnath-paaneah.

H6848.definition:
from an unused root meaning to extrude;
a viper (as thrusting out the tongue, i.e. hissing)
KJV: adder, cockatrice.

H6849.definition:
feminine from the same as H6848 (צֶפַע);
an outcast thing
KJV: issue.

H6850.definition:
a primitive root;
to coo or chirp (as a bird)
KJV: chatter, peep, whisper.

H6851.definition:
from H6687 (צוּף);
a willow (as growing in overflowed places)
KJV: willow tree.

H6852.definition:
a primitive root;
to skip about, i.e. return
KJV: depart early.

H6853.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6833 (צִפּוֹר);
a bird.
KJV: bird.

H6854.definition:
from H6852 (צָפַר) and a word elsewhere unused meaning a swamp;
a marsh-leaper, i.e. frog
KJV: frog.

H6855.definition:
feminine of H6833 (צִפּוֹר); bird;
Tsipporah, Moses' wife
KJV: Zipporah.

H6856.definition:
from H6852 (צָפַר) (in the denominative sense (from H6833 (צִפּוֹר)) of scratching);
properly, a claw, i.e. (human) nail; also the point of astyle (or pen, tipped with adamant)
KJV: nail, point.

H6857.definition:
from H6822 (צָפָה); watch-tower;
Tsephath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zephath.

H6858.definition:
from an unused root meaning to encircle;
a capital of a column
KJV: chapiter.

H6859.definition:
the same as H6857 (צְפַת);
Tsephathah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zephathah.

H6860.definition:
or צִיקלַג; (1 Chronicles 12:1,20), of uncertain derivation;
Tsiklag or Tsikelag, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ziklag.

H6861.definition:
from an unused root meaning to wind;
a sack (as tied at the mouth)
KJV: husk.

H6863.definition:
from H6887 (צָרַר); rock;
Tser, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zer.

H6864.definition:
from H6696 (צוּר);
a stone (as if pressed hard or to a point); (by implication, of use) a knife
KJV: flint, sharp stone.

H6865.definition:
or צוֹר; the same as H6864 (צֹר); a rock;
Tsor, a place in Palestine
KJV: Tyre, Tyrus.

H6866.definition:
a primitive root;
to burn
KJV: burn.

H6867.definition:
from H6686 (צוּעָר);
conflagration (of fire or disease)
KJV: burning, inflammation.

H6868.definition:
or צְרֵדָתָה; apparently from an unused root meaning to pierce; puncture;
Tseredah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zereda, Zeredathah.

H6869.definition:
feminine of H6862 (צַר);
tightness (i.e. figuratively, trouble); transitively, a female rival:
KJV: adversary, adversity, affliction, anguish, distress, tribulation, trouble.

H6870.definition:
feminine passive participle from the same as H6875 (צְרִי); wounded;
Tserujah, an Israelitess
KJV: Zeruiah.

H6871.definition:
feminine passive participle of H6879 (צָרַע); leprous;
Tseruah, an Israelitess
KJV: Zeruah.

H6872.definition:
or (shorter) צְרֹר; from H6887 (צָרַר);
a parcel (as packed up); also a kernel or particle (as if a package)
KJV: bag, [idiom] bendeth, bundle, least grain, small stone.

H6873.definition:
a primitive root;
to be clear (in tone, i.e. shrill), i.e. to whoop
KJV: cry, roar.

H6874.definition:
the same as H6875 (צְרִי);
Tseri, an Israelite
KJV: Zeri. Compare H3340 (יִצְרִי).

H6875.definition:
or צֳרִי; from an unused root meaning to crack (as by pressure), hence, to leak;
distillation, i.e. balsam
KJV: balm.

H6876.definition:
patrial from H6865 (צֹר);
a Tsorite or inhabitant of Tsor (i.e. Syrian)
KJV: (man) of Tyre.

H6877.definition:
from H6873 (צָרַח) in the sense of clearness of vision;
a citadel
KJV: high place, hold.

H6878.definition:
from an unused root meaning to need;
need
KJV: need.

H6879.definition:
a primitive root;
to scourge, i.e. (intransitive and figurative) to be stricken with leprosy
KJV: leper, leprous.

H6880.definition:
from H6879 (צָרַע);
a wasp (as stinging)
KJV: hornet.

H6881.definition:
apparently another form for H6880 (צִרְעָה);
Tsorah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zareah, Zorah, Zoreah.

H6882.definition:
or צׇרְעָתִי; patrial from H6881 (צׇרְעָה);
a Tsorite or Tsorathite, i.e. inhabitants of Tsorah
KJV: Zorites, Zareathites, Zorathites.

H6884.definition:
a primitive root;
to fuse (metal), i.e. refine (literally or figuratively)
KJV: cast, (re-) fine(-er), founder, goldsmith, melt, pure, purge away, try.

H6885.definition:
from H6884 (צָרַף); refiner;
Tsorephi (with the article), an Israelite
KJV: goldsmith's.

H6886.definition:
from H6884 (צָרַף); refinement;
Tsarephath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zarephath.

H6887.definition:
a primitive root;
to cramp, literally or figuratively, transitive or intransitive
KJV: adversary, (be in) afflict(-ion), beseige, bind (up), (be in, bring) distress, enemy, narrower, oppress, pangs, shut up, be in a strait (trouble), vex.

H6888.definition:
apparently by erroneous transcription for H6868 (צְרֵדָה);
Tsererah for Tseredah
KJV: Zererath.

H6889.definition:
perhaps from H6671 (צָהַר); splendor;
Tsereth, an Israelite
KJV: Zereth.

H6890.definition:
from the same as H6889 (צֶרֶת) and H7837 (שַׁחַר) with the article interposed; splendor of the dawn;
Tsereth-hash-Shachar, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zareth-shahar.

H6891.definition:
perhaps for H6868 (צְרֵדָה);
Tsarethan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Zarthan. q

H6892.definition:
or קִיא; from H6958 (קוֹא);
vomit
KJV: vomit.

H6893.definition:
from H6958 (קוֹא);
probably the pelican (from vomiting)
KJV: cormorant.

H6894.definition:
from H6895 (קָבַב);
a hollow, i.e. vessel used as a (dry) measure
KJV: cab.

H6895.definition:
a primitive root;
to scoop out, i.e. (figuratively) to malign or execrate (i.e. stab with words)
KJV: [idiom] at all, curse.

H6896.definition:
from H6895 (קָבַב);
the paunch (as a cavity) or first stomach of ruminants
KJV: maw.

H6897.definition:
from H6895 (קָבַב);
the abdomen (as a cavity)
KJV: belly.

H6898.definition:
from H6895 (קָבַב);
a pavilion (as a domed cavity)
KJV: tent.

H6899.definition:
from H6908 (קָבַץ);
a throng
KJV: company.
